  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1241 AM MDT Mon Jul 6 2026\n\nA downtrend in diurnal shower and thunderstorm coverage favoring the \nhigher terrain begins Wednesday with the flattened 596 dam 500 \nmb upper high over southern CA and northern Baja CA. Even lower \ncoverage of diurnal showers and storms across the higher terrain and \nnearby highlands Thursday with the flattened upper near still over \nsouthern CA. With the lowering storm coverage, high temperatures \nwill heat up a little compared to earlier in the week with 90s to \nlow 100s common across lower elevations. A few zones, like the NW \nPlateau, middle and lower RGV, and Chaves County Plains will need to \nbe monitored for potential Heat Advisories.\n\nThe monsoon high shifts back east towards the state Friday to over \nthe central Rockies this weekend while also strengthening to around \n600 dam at 500 mb. This will help keep shower and storm chances \nfavoring the higher terrain on the lower end. The one exception \nlooks to be across northeast NM Friday afternoon and evening due to \na disturbance moving southeast among the northwest flow of the \nupper high circulation centered over AZ. Temperatures will be hot \nacross lower elevations with highs in the 90s to around 100.",
